  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${A}^{\u2032}$, the image of $A(-1,1)$ under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $A$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $A:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${A}^{\u2032}.$ Therefore, ${A}^{\u2032}(2,1).$",
